MODIFICATIONS
------------------------------------------------------------------------------

This repository is a fork maintained by Mad Pony Interactive. It is based on
`comfyui-melodramabox` version 2.1.0 as published to the ComfyUI Registry
(https://registry.comfy.org/nodes/comfyui-melodramabox). The upstream source
repository named in that release's pyproject.toml,
https://github.com/doggeddalle/ComfyUI-MelodramaBox, returns 404, so the
changes below could not be contributed upstream.

The following files were modified. Each change is marked in place with an
`MPI-607` (items 1-3) or `MPI-1008` (item 4) comment.

1. dramabox_nodes/downloader.py
   `ensure_text_encoder` inspected only the FIRST registered `text_encoders`
   root. Roots added via extra_model_paths.yaml are appended to that list and
   never prepended, so a shared model store was invisible and the pack would
   re-download the ~8 GB Gemma-3 snapshot even when it was already present.
   Now every registered root is checked before downloading.

2. dramabox_nodes/loaders.py
   The documented `.gguf` DiT workflow could not be selected. ComfyUI's
   `supported_pt_extensions` does not contain `.gguf`, so
   `get_filename_list("diffusion_models")` can never return one, and the
   loader's dropdown was therefore always empty of GGUF files. Now the
   registered roots are scanned directly. Deliberately NOT fixed by adding
   `.gguf` to `supported_pt_extensions`, which is a global shared by every
   installed node pack.

3. dramabox_nodes/model_management.py
   `DramaBoxUnloadModels` defined no `IS_CHANGED`, so ComfyUI served it from
   cache and the unload silently never ran. The node exists only for its side
   effect, so a cached result is always wrong. It now declares `IS_CHANGED`
   and re-executes every run.

4. dramabox_nodes/model/patcher.py
   `load_patchers` let ComfyUI partially load a model when VRAM was short.
   ComfyUI's partial load only offloads comfy.ops cast layers, and no DramaBox
   module uses them, so the weights that missed the budget stayed on the CPU
   and the next forward failed with "Expected all tensors to be on the same
   device" (seen in DramaBoxTextEncode after the 4-bit Gemma took the VRAM).
   It now always requests a full load.

